{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1089327-how-to-create-a-modern-god","id":1089327,"title":"How to create a Modern God?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-07T12:58:53-07:00","id":1089327,"title":"How to create a Modern God?","content":"Been talking with some friends after i introduced them to Scion and American Gods.<br /> <br /> So i been thinking, how does one Idea becomes a God? or rather how a concept would evolve into a god within the Scion game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:20:44-07:00","id":1089340,"title":"","content":"Two gods get together and interact. Sometimes they have sex, sometimes they just mingle together, sometimes one ejaculates on the other and the other brushes it off uncomfortably and it spawns a new entity on its own, sometimes the heavens and the earth meet and things just happen. Almost anything you can reasonably think of can result in a new god.<br /> <br /> How gods become supernaturally connected to ideas depends incredibly on the culture they are representing (or trying to emulate). Some gods are just born connected to an idea, while others have a personality that is close to an idea and they get connected by coincidence or circumstance. Others are outright given their ideas and told to manage them, while some have no supernatural connection to ideas at all.<br /> <br /> So it basically comes down to &quot;<b>However you want. Just make it an interesting story.</b>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:28:18-07:00","id":1089343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1089327-how-to-create-a-modern-god#post1089327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been talking with some friends after i introduced them to Scion and American Gods.<br /> <br /> So i been thinking, how does one Idea becomes a God? or rather how a concept would evolve into a god within the Scion game?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well Scion, at least with regard to &quot;the World&quot; setting, doesn't work like American Gods setting. It's not about belief just creating beings wherever some form of worship is directed. There needs to be a narrative, a Legend. So as Incendax, said its usually via some form of creation by existing divinities.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, you're unlikely to see a Pantheon like the &quot;New Gods&quot; of American Gods in &quot;the World&quot; as not only the metaphysics work off of Legend, not Worship, but also the &quot;Old Gods&quot; have adapted much better than in the American Gods setting. You don't need a new God of Media when Hermes has adapted perfectly well to the modern age, for example.<br /> <br /> But of course, that's only in &quot;the World&quot;, a setting Shard with a Pantheon of Gods of Modernity facing off against the ancient gods as an American Gods homage is totally plausible!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:34:39-07:00","id":1089346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1089327-how-to-create-a-modern-god#post1089327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been talking with some friends after i introduced them to Scion and American Gods.<br /> <br /> So i been thinking, how does one Idea becomes a God? or rather how a concept would evolve into a god within the Scion game?</div> </div> </div> </div>In a Scion game? Well, the way it would work in Scion 1e is that a existing Deity would have a Scion child, and that child could attach themselves to a modern concept, and uplift it along with themselves during Apotheosis.<br /> <br /> Scion doesn't use the idea of belief uplifting concepts into Deities independently, as we see in American Gods. However, a Scion could very easily adopt modern concepts and bring those into the divine fold rather easily. A modern War God could bring in the concept of Artillery, Special Forces, or Submarines. A Scion who is an artist could become a literal Rock God, etc.<br /> <br /> To use an example from American Gods, but a very background one as to not spoil anything for folks watching the show, I'll use the Railway Gods eluded to a few times. They could have been Scions of any Deity, it doesn't really matter, but let's say Hermes since he is a well known Traveler. One of these Scions could have been a Railway Engineer, another an Immigrant Worker (I don't know a ton about the American railway, but up in Canada they would probably be a Shen or Tuatha Scion depending on which side of the country they were on), and a third a corporate railway baron.<br /> <br /> The Railway Engineer has Epic Intelligence, Forge (not actually in RAW, but a common houseruled Purview), Fire, and Water. They bring about huge developments in the world of the steam engine, and through various complex adventures eventually reach Legend 9 and undergo Apotheosis. Now you have a God of the Steam Engine.<br /> <br /> The Immigrant Worker has Epic Stamina, Epic Strength, Death (since so many people perished in the construction and were buried around the tracks or inside side tunnels), and Psychopomp (since they came from far-afield and help others travel). They carve tunnels through mountains, hammer railway spikes in with their bare hands, lift entire rails by themselves, and gently bury the mortals alongside them who perish during the construction of the Iron Road. For this, let's say they are Shen. They undergo Apotheosis, and join the Celestial Bureaucracy, being appointed a position within one of the myriad ministries of Heaven, and are appointed as the Deity in charge of Railways.<br /> <br /> The Corporate Railway Baron is another Scion. They have Epic Charisma, Epic Manipulation, Wealth (not actually in RAW, but sometimes houseruled in), and Psychopomp. Their industries forge railways across the entire continent, and are an industry leader. They provide massive numbers of jobs, mostly poor paying, taking advantage of immigrant laborers coming to North America. They reshape the nation under their thumb, wielding tremendous influence upon the State, and go on many adventures which leads to their Apotheosis upon reaching Legend 9. They join their Pantheon as the God of Industry, or Railways, or in general probably has a wide 'Divine Portfolio.'<br /> <br /> So that's how it would work in Scion! A concept doesn't independently become a God in Scion, but a Scion can 'pick them up', and become the Deity of that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T16:04:05-07:00","id":1089441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1089327-how-to-create-a-modern-god#post1089327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been talking with some friends after i introduced them to Scion and American Gods.<br /> <br /> So i been thinking, how does one Idea becomes a God? or rather how a concept would evolve into a god within the Scion game?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The hardest part for me is thinking up a divine name for those who make the cut. English is the only language I speak, and I have little information on how the naming schemes of other cultures work. The only thing I can think of is to take an example from the pre-made scions and borrow one of their parent's alternate titles. Like Eric taking the name Donar from Thor. But this seems uninspired and could be seen as confusing at times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T16:20:43-07:00","id":1089448,"title":"","content":"Wait wait..so its impossible to have &quot; The Dude &quot; (Lebowski) or hell, even Ronald McDonalds as a god? (i hate my players for suggesting those two)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T16:30:07-07:00","id":1089458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1089327-how-to-create-a-modern-god?p=1089448#post1089448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait wait..so its impossible to have &quot; The Dude &quot; (Lebowski) or hell, even Ronald McDonalds as a god? (i hate my players for suggesting those two)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a Scion could like... adopt themselves into that role? But no, those abstract ideas do not 'become' Gods in Scion. A Scion could declare that they want to be &quot;The Dude,&quot; theoretically though. But the notion of 'The Dude' from The Big Lebowski can not 'create itself' as a Deity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T16:37:34-07:00","id":1089464,"title":"","content":"Gods in scion are actual honest to god (ha), fire and brimstone Deities. They do not really operate on the notion that they are dependent on and originate from humanity, or are some kind of Oneiric gestalt consciousness, not even in the Jungian sense. (I suppose there is nothing stopping you from doing that, but it would be the equivalent of a shard setting, which i think scion 2e is actually going to support).<br /> <br /> As such, no, Ronald McDonald could not be a God, nor could &quot;The Dude&quot;.<br /> <br /> You could conceivably have a deity or scion be born that somewhat resembles these people or concepts, but that no more likely or relevant as some random person happening to be kinda like &quot;the Dude&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T09:36:06-07:00","id":1089833,"title":"","content":"(Note: I know nutting about the new ed) Is it possible to uplift a mortal hero, not so much Hercules who was half-divine, but basically all-mortal like Jason or Daedalus? Not sure if that was in the 1E rules or a houserule. Seems like some version of that (give the mortal some ambrosia and bam they are semidivine) would be reasonable. So if you found someone who was the mortal ideal of &quot;the Dude&quot; ness. Or grab Jerry Springer or Rupert Murdock and promote them to a media-type god.<br /> <br /> Also as a possible inspiration look up the book &quot;The Gods of War&quot;, edited by Stasheff. Short story collection, frame story being the creation of a techno-war-god. Too much &quot;belief creates gods&quot; for the basic setting, but it does cover some of the &quot;how the other gods react to a newcomer&quot;. And could probably work well in an American Gods-type shard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T09:58:34-07:00","id":1089840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpoonR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1089327-how-to-create-a-modern-god?p=1089833#post1089833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Note: I know nutting about the new ed) Is it possible to uplift a mortal hero, not so much Hercules who was half-divine, but basically all-mortal like Jason or Daedalus? Not sure if that was in the 1E rules or a houserule. Seems like some version of that (give the mortal some ambrosia and bam they are semidivine) would be reasonable. So if you found someone who was the mortal ideal of &quot;the Dude&quot; ness. Or grab Jerry Springer or Rupert Murdock and promote them to a media-type god.<br /> <br /> Also as a possible inspiration look up the book &quot;The Gods of War&quot;, edited by Stasheff. Short story collection, frame story being the creation of a techno-war-god. Too much &quot;belief creates gods&quot; for the basic setting, but it does cover some of the &quot;how the other gods react to a newcomer&quot;. And could probably work well in an American Gods-type shard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there was any way to do that in base 1e... 2e on the other hand has a Chosen Origin, but I'm not sure how open ended that is... as far as I remember initially only people under a very special set of circumstances could be chosen, but I <i>think</i> that requirement got loosened later, but don't quote me on that.<br /> <br /> Also, Created Scions are a thing now, beings like Enkidu or Pandora or Ganesha who are literally sculpted by Gods into existence... not sure if the character you are referring to woudl fit this though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T11:20:20-07:00","id":1089867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpoonR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1089327-how-to-create-a-modern-god?p=1089833#post1089833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Note: I know nutting about the new ed) Is it possible to uplift a mortal hero, not so much Hercules who was half-divine, but basically all-mortal like Jason or Daedalus? Not sure if that was in the 1E rules or a houserule. Seems like some version of that (give the mortal some ambrosia and bam they are semidivine) would be reasonable. So if you found someone who was the mortal ideal of &quot;the Dude&quot; ness. Or grab Jerry Springer or Rupert Murdock and promote them to a media-type god.<br /> <br /> Also as a possible inspiration look up the book &quot;The Gods of War&quot;, edited by Stasheff. Short story collection, frame story being the creation of a techno-war-god. Too much &quot;belief creates gods&quot; for the basic setting, but it does cover some of the &quot;how the other gods react to a newcomer&quot;. And could probably work well in an American Gods-type shard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actually in 2nd edition, you don't strictly have to be the child of a God to become a Scion. It's possible for anyone (or anything) to become a Scion if they earn the God's favor. That means you can have animals or even objects manifesting divine powers. Although I'm not entirely sure how inanimate Scions work.<br /> <br /> <br /> My guess is that Scion objects possess whoever holds them and uses their body to act as a medium for their power. Sort of like a living weapon that takes control of whoever's wielding it.<br /> <br /> <br /> While we're on the topic of belief creating gods, that's also how it works in the Black and White series of games. When a godless mortal offers a prayer of true need, a god is born into existence who quickly comes to answer their plea. Of course the mortal has absolutely no control over what kind of deity they've just spawned into existence, which means they could end up making their situation worse than it was before!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-08-2017, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T05:31:55-07:00","id":1091076,"title":"","content":"I've always disliked the 'belief creating gods' idea in fantasy works as it makes the gods lesser and ephemeral when they are meant to be immortal and elemental. it just feels somehow less interesting and a bit egotistical for humanity to make gods.<br /> <br /> However the idea of newer scions modeling themselves after modern ideas is really cool. A child of Hermes could easily do the whole god of media thing, and i've had an idea for awhile now for a son of Heracles who decided that the morals and ideology of the older gods are obsolete and is trying to turn himself into a superman style god of heroism (mainly epic attributes and sky purviews) under the logic that comics are the modern mythology and deserving of respect. It'd be easy to make both Player and Non-Player scions who are reinterpreting their divinity under a modern lens<br /> <br /> As to creating them basically it amounts to building a scion's legend until the transcend mortality. So Modern style gods wouldn't be hard to interject, as a GM you just need to have a group of scions who have reached godhood at the time the game begins. I believe the companion will have rules for making your own pantheons and Scion: god will have them as playeable characters with the existing purview giving you an idea of how their powers should work (Forge should cover most tech needs for a science god for example)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 05-11-2017, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T19:50:13-07:00","id":1091393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1089327-how-to-create-a-modern-god?p=1091076#post1091076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...i've had an idea for awhile now for a son of Heracles who decided that the morals and ideology of the older gods are obsolete and is trying to turn himself into a superman style god of heroism (mainly epic attributes and sky purviews) under the logic that comics are the modern mythology and deserving of respect...</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you're making me think of a scion of Hades that specifically sets out to hijack the legend of Batman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","name":"Meribson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T17:59:53-07:00","id":1094368,"title":"","content":"I would hardly call the comic books deserving of respect when it comes to heroes. Classical heroes got the job done and made sure the villains stayed down. Modern day heroes only treat the symptoms, not the cause. And the villains keep coming back to cause more mayhem. If a comic book hero tried to seal away the Titans again, chances are Fate would have them break right back out and you'd have to do the whole process over again. Then they'd break out, you'd put them back in, they'd break out, <b>it would be a never ending cycle of pain and misery.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I'm a fan of the trope of Gods being sustained by the power of belief, but humanity largely being unaware of it. It gives the possibility for stories in which mortals finally realize they're sick of being pushed around and try to rebel against the divinities; and actually having a fighting chance at doing so. In settings where the Gods are eternal and elemental, it means that mortals are pretty much stuck being their playthings. Makes it hard to empathize with or care about the plight of mortals if a Scion's life is objectively more valuable than theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T17:44:30-07:00","id":1097643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1089327-how-to-create-a-modern-god?p=1094368#post1094368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would hardly call the comic books deserving of respect when it comes to heroes. Classical heroes got the job done and made sure the villains stayed down. Modern day heroes only treat the symptoms, not the cause. And the villains keep coming back to cause more mayhem. If a comic book hero tried to seal away the Titans again, chances are Fate would have them break right back out and you'd have to do the whole process over again. Then they'd break out, you'd put them back in, they'd break out, <b>it would be a never ending cycle of pain and misery.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, things are a bit more complicated than that.<br /> <br /> For one, when the Superheroes stop a major story arc, they generally <i>stop it</i>. I.e., if the Superheroes manage to stop the Alien Invasion, the Aliens are still out there but the Invasion Attempt has been thwarted and it won't come again in exactly the same form. Hell, that &quot;in the same form&quot; is another important little rule,-- but let's get back to that later,-- because really the &quot;Alien Invasion&quot; rule is kind of where the Titanic-level Threats would rise. So, Superheroes COULD stuff Titan's back in Tartarus. They'd still be there, ready to cause trouble again in some other form, but they could 'save the day' in the current threat. The real issue is generally more in terms of the day to day rivals of the Superheroes, their &quot;Rogues Gallery&quot;, who Fate will conspire to ensure they're not permanently taken out of the picture. But, this is more likely to be other Gods and what not as opposed to huge world-ending threats.<br /> <br /> Another important point, honestly, is the one that I brushed up against earlier. Mainly, threats that a Superhero defeats don't tend to come again in the same form. Once you thwart a villain, it doesn't matter how successful that plan was or how much damage was done, the next time he acts? It'll be in a novel fashion that doesn't really draw on past attempts. If you stop a villain from doing this one specific thing, you don't have to worry about them just... doing it again.. even if logically they <i>really, really should</i>. This is important for the big stories, like titan's breaking out of Tartarus, and also for the smaller ones, like the Joker kidnapping and maiming one of your followers.<br /> <br /> Last, and perhaps most important, the core conceit of Superheroes is less that they don't actually solve problems or anything. No, it's the fact that their lives tend to be on repeat, that eventually things are going to circle back around and you're going to end up telling the tale all over again from the beginning. Superheroes don't get old, they don't really reach any real climax in their tales, they just kind of run on for a while and then start all over again. They're forever trapped in the beginning stages of their &quot;careers&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T18:29:10-07:00","id":1097650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrownedSun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1089327-how-to-create-a-modern-god?p=1097643#post1097643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, things are a bit more complicated than that.<br /> <br /> For one, when the Superheroes stop a major story arc, they generally <i>stop it</i>. I.e., if the Superheroes manage to stop the Alien Invasion, the Aliens are still out there but the Invasion Attempt has been thwarted and it won't come again in exactly the same form. Hell, that &quot;in the same form&quot; is another important little rule,-- but let's get back to that later,-- because really the &quot;Alien Invasion&quot; rule is kind of where the Titanic-level Threats would rise. So, Superheroes COULD stuff Titan's back in Tartarus. They'd still be there, ready to cause trouble again in some other form, but they could 'save the day' in the current threat. The real issue is generally more in terms of the day to day rivals of the Superheroes, their &quot;Rogues Gallery&quot;, who Fate will conspire to ensure they're not permanently taken out of the picture. But, this is more likely to be other Gods and what not as opposed to huge world-ending threats.<br /> <br /> Another important point, honestly, is the one that I brushed up against earlier. Mainly, threats that a Superhero defeats don't tend to come again in the same form. Once you thwart a villain, it doesn't matter how successful that plan was or how much damage was done, the next time he acts? It'll be in a novel fashion that doesn't really draw on past attempts. If you stop a villain from doing this one specific thing, you don't have to worry about them just... doing it again.. even if logically they <i>really, really should</i>. This is important for the big stories, like titan's breaking out of Tartarus, and also for the smaller ones, like the Joker kidnapping and maiming one of your followers.<br /> <br /> Last, and perhaps most important, the core conceit of Superheroes is less that they don't actually solve problems or anything. No, it's the fact that their lives tend to be on repeat, that eventually things are going to circle back around and you're going to end up telling the tale all over again from the beginning. Superheroes don't get old, they don't really reach any real climax in their tales, they just kind of run on for a while and then start all over again. They're forever trapped in the beginning stages of their &quot;careers&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The problem with super hero comics is that they lean towards the side of extremism when it comes to their ideals and philosophies. A Hero can't simply be an advocate of the death penalty in regards to the most evil or dangerous criminals, no. The Hero has to become a ruthless, dictating psychopath who believes that any and all crimes are worthy of death. They go completely off the rails in their efforts to show that killing is wrong, and in so doing, they miss the point entirely.<br /> <br /> Conversely, if a Hero promotes the sanctity of life, then that generally means they have to preserve <b>all life</b>, even the living war crimes who slaughter people by the thousands just for shits and giggles. In trying to preserve the minority, they effectively put the majority in mortal danger time and time again. In real life this would not be tolerated. 90% of these criminals would have been sentenced to life, or death within their first appearance. But in the wonderful world of comic books, they come away with little more than a slap on the wrist!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T19:59:01-07:00","id":1097672,"title":"","content":"Those villains do get life sentences, they just break out again. Granted after the third time you might argue they ought skip the life sentence and go straight to death, but it's not like legislatures are known for reacting to anything quickly. Not hard to imagine them avoiding it just by virtue of no politician being willing to be the one who introduces the bill to make killing them legal.<br /> <br /> Also super (or mythic) powered villains might not always be as easy as that to kill. Particularly once you start hitting god levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","name":"MalicWanderer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T20:58:02-07:00","id":1097682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalicWanderer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1089327-how-to-create-a-modern-god?p=1097672#post1097672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those villains do get life sentences, they just break out again. Granted after the third time you might argue they ought skip the life sentence and go straight to death, but it's not like legislatures are known for reacting to anything quickly. Not hard to imagine them avoiding it just by virtue of no politician being willing to be the one who introduces the bill to make killing them legal.<br /> <br /> Also super (or mythic) powered villains might not always be as easy as that to kill. Particularly once you start hitting god levels.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Who says they have to make it to court? I'm pretty sure it's legal to kill in self defense, especially when you've got a super powered criminal leveling a death ray at your face. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But the point I was trying to make is that if the Heroes tried to impersonate the modern day interpretation of heroism; it would only cause more problems than it would solve. Particularly if Fate decides to help them reenact the roles they aspire to fulfill. The Titanspawn would become an invincible adversary; one whom the Heroes could not bring themselves to destroy outright, but rather banish them for a time, where they would inevitably return to cause more havoc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-28-2017, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}